<description>
Complete a four-corner framed rectangle from one decorated anchor rectangle and its diagonal mate.

Input structure:
- The background is the dominant color.
- Two same-color solid rectangular anchors of the same size sit on opposite
  diagonal corners, with the first anchor above-left of the second.
- The upper-left anchor has two one-cell-thick vertical control bars to its
  right and two one-cell-thick horizontal control bars below it.

Rule:
- Copy the anchor rectangle into the two missing corners of the implied
  larger rectangle.
- Repeat the right-side control bars horizontally between the left and right
  anchors, using their spacing as the period, and draw the outer top and
  bottom borders in the first right-control color.
- Repeat the below-side control bars vertically between the top and bottom
  anchors, using the same period, and draw the outer left and right borders
  in the first below-control color.

Key insight: The small control bars are the first two ticks of two periodic
frame patterns; the diagonal anchor supplies the opposite corner and the
missing two anchor copies.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "two same-color solid rectangular anchors, with two right control bars and two below control bars beside the upper-left anchor",
  "dst": "the missing two anchor corners and periodic frame segments between all four anchors",
  "transform": "copy the anchor rectangle into the missing corners; repeat the right-control colors across the top and bottom anchor rows and outer borders, and repeat the below-control colors down the left and right side bars using the same spacing"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 16-30 rows x 16-30 cols, single bg color (any of 0-9)
  colors: 5 distinct non-bg colors — anchor, right1, right2, below1, below2; right2 == below2 [observed]
  anchors:
    shape: solid square 1x1 to 4x4 [observed square], same color, same size
    placement: two anchors on a diagonal — source upper-left, dest lower-right
    margin: source top-left at (sr0, sc0) with sr0 >= 1, sc0 >= 1; dest bottom-right at (dr1, dc1) with dr1 <= nrows-2, dc1 <= ncols-2
  control_bars:
    right: 2 vertical 1-cell-wide bars to right of source, same height as anchor
    below: 2 horizontal 1-cell-tall bars below source, same width as anchor
    offsets: always [1, 3] from anchor edge (step=2, period=4)
    right colors [right1, right2], below colors [below1, below2] — all 4 distinct from anchor
  gap_constraint: horizontal gap (dc0 - sc1 - 1) = 4*Nh + 1, vertical gap (dr0 - sr1 - 1) = 4*Nv + 1
  repetitions: Nh, Nv in 2-4 independently
  output_structure: |
    4 anchor copies at corners of implied rectangle; top/bottom horizontal frames
    with periodic [right1, bg, right2, bg] pattern and outer border in right1;
    left/right vertical frames with periodic [below1, bg, below2, bg] pattern
    and outer border in below1. Structure size = (2*ah + 4*Nv + 3) x (2*aw + 4*Nh + 3).

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick bg, 4 non-bg colors (anchor, right1, right2, below1; set below2 = right2).
    2. Pick anchor size S in 1-4 (square), Nh in 2-4, Nv in 2-4.
    3. Compute structure size = (2S + 4Nv + 3) x (2S + 4Nh + 3).
    4. Pick grid size >= structure size + (1,1) for minimum margin; add random extra margin on each side (0-3).
    5. Place source anchor at (sr0, sc0) where sr0 >= 1, sc0 >= 1.
    6. Compute dest anchor position from gaps = 4*N + 1; verify dest fits with margin >= 1 from bottom-right edge.
    7. Build input — place source anchor, dest anchor, 2 right control bars at offsets 1 and 3, 2 below control bars at offsets 1 and 3. Rest is bg.
    8. Verify by running solver; output should match the full framed rectangle.
